My knight ascended last night.  I have to say the end game is very
convenient for a knight.  Riding a ki-rin is oh so nice.  Lava? no
problem, just fly over it.  Spiked pit?  no problem, just fly over
it.  Pet get zapped? no problem, its "oR will bounce it back.  Pet get
injured?  no problem, the invisible saddled ki-rin feels better.  The
only (relatively minor) nuisances are eating corpses and entering
shops, but that's very minor compared to juggling a ring of
levitation.

The magic mirror is also a useful quest artifact:  level 30 magic
missile becomes an instakill for most monsters.

I thought the jousting would be more useful than it turned out for
me.  My first lance broke at some point, so I started twoweaponing a
+7 silver saber before I could polypile a new lance.  Between lance
only, lance + silver saber, Excalibur + lance, or Excalibur + silver
saber, I don't know which combination is best.  The +7 lance as a
primary weapon is nice for killing eels at distance, I guess.  Against
dangerous monsters, I think the knight wants to use magic missile over
melee, so I'm not sure the lance is all that important for its stun
effect.  The lance is remarkably heavy.  If I ever play a knight
again, I'll stash it early in the box where I put most of my apples
and carrots.  I thought pushing priests back + jumping boots would
make Astral a lot easier.  but pushing them back only works if there's
nobody behind them, and with them summoning insects and all, it seemed
easier to just magic missile the priests rather than try to jump
around them.
In the end, jousting seemed to me like a marginal benefit, not a game
changer.

I just started playing a barbarian.  The early game seems like a
breeze compared to the knight games.  So far (through Mine Town), I
haven't had to write Elbereth once as a barbarian; I just swing my
weapon(s) and watch my foes die.  That wasn't working with my Dx:8
knights.

After I try out some more roles, I will edit the wiki and most likely
move Knights up in difficulty.  Having a fighter start with the worst
Dexterity and worst Constitution of any role is a big problem in the
early game that just isn't offset by a saddle, lance, knight jump, and
18 charisma.


